    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c342cd4b",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: what_women_think_theyll_do_when_the_economy_collapses_vs_what_theyll_actually_do; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a woman with a shocked, fearful expression, hands covering her mouth, juxtaposed with the text 'what women think they'll do when the economy collapses vs what they'll actually do.' This visual and textual combination implies that women are irrational, hysterical, or overly emotional in crisis situations, reinforcing a misogynistic stereotype that women are 'crazy' or 'hysterical' when faced with economic hardship. The intent is to mock or belittle women by suggesting their reactions are disproportionate or irrational, fitting within the 'Mysogynous' toxicity category as it targets women based on gendered stereotypes of emotional instability and irrationality.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0158a02e"
